    "title": "Why Daniel Cormier's 'real heavyweight' claim involving Tom Aspinall played out after 'tough challenge' prediction - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Adnan Riaz ,\n1 hours ago\nTom Aspinall and Alex Pereira on stage at the UFC 295 press conference. Credit: Chris Unger/Zuffa LLC via Getty Images Daniel Cormier’s major point featured British MMA star Tom Aspinall at the heart of it and showed the standout detail about the UFC’s current heavyweight division.\nTom Aspinall has been out of the octagon since his first UFC heavyweight title defence ended in a no-contest result against Ciryl Gane at UFC 321 in 2025.\nCiryl Gane accidentally poked Aspinall in the eye and the 33-year-old heavyweight champion was unable to continue beyond the first round at the Etihad Arena.\nAspinall had surgery on both of his eyes in early 2026 for a rare condition that he had and the Salford-born fighter is now targeting a return to the MMA octagon.\nREAD MORE: Tom Aspinall is going full villain for his UFC return: ‘No more Mr. Nice Guy’ Daniel Cormier singled out Tom Aspinall for the challenge that Alex Pereira faced against Ciryl Gane Tom Aspinall revealed late last month that he had been cleared to return to “full training” and was in “talks” with the UFC over his rematch with Ciryl Gane .\nGane set up a second encounter with Aspinall after the 36-year-old French UFC star won the interim heavyweight title against Alex Pereira at UFC Freedom 250 .\nAlex Pereira made his debut at heavyweight and the 38-year-old Brazilian MMA fighter suffered a second-round TKO defeat to Gane at the White House-hosted event.\nSpeaking ahead of the UFC Freedom 250 card, which was recently uploaded to YouTube , Daniel Cormier explained that Gane was a “real heavyweight” in his eyes.\nCormier added that Gane was the toughest test that Pereira could have taken for his heavyweight debut outside of facing UFC title holder Aspinall.\n“He’s [Gane] a real heavyweight,” he told MMA fans during a live Q&A in June.\n“So, if he goes out there and he fights like a real heavyweight, it’s a tough challenge for Alex.\n“It really is the hardest fight for him in the division outside of Tom Aspinall. And that’s why you see the betting line where it is, where Ciryl Gane is actually a favorite.”\nREAD MORE: Eddie Hearn signs Ian Machado Garry after making Tom Aspinall $1M outside the UFC UFC legend Daniel Cormier pinpointed the huge difference between Alex Pereira and Ciryl Gane Cormier was asked how he would have coached Gane for the Pereira fight at UFC White House had he been in the interim heavyweight champion’s corner.\nThe 47-year-old UFC legend claimed that the scales were already tipped in Gane’s favour because of his weight going into the Pereira encounter last month.\n“And if I’m Ciryl Gane, I’m just telling him to be exactly who he’s been,” he explained.\n“He’s a heavyweight, man. I said this the other day to Alex. I go… or Ciryl [and] I said, ‘When was the last time you weighed?’ I said 84 kilos because they’re, you know, French kilos?”\n“He [Gane] goes, ‘I was 15.’ I said, ‘Pereira made that weight two years ago.’ Ciryl Gane has not weighed 185 pounds since he was 15 years old. He’s 37 now — 22 years [ago], he’s a real heavyweight.”\nA rematch between Gane and Aspinall for the UFC heavyweight title has not been officially confirmed, despite being in the works at the moment.",
    "summary": "Credit: Chris Unger/Zuffa LLC via Getty Images Daniel Cormier’s major point featured British MMA star Tom Aspinall at the heart of it and showed the standout detail about the UFC’s current heavyweight division. Alex Pereira made his debut at heavyweight and the 38-year-old Brazilian MMA fighter suffered a second-round TKO defeat to Gane at the White House-hosted event. Speaking ahead of the UFC Freedom 250 card, which was recently uploaded to YouTube , Daniel Cormier explained that Gane was a “real heavyweight” in his eyes.",
